d=21790 -> 0 rows; the 5 % tolerance exists only as a repo constant (scoring.py:33) and in prose", "remediation": "register the case row (case_name cavity_re3200_ghia, metric max|err|/U_lid pointwise, tolerance 5 %, ref_source Ghia 1982 Table I/II Re=3200, status pending) so the gate can adjudicate"}, {"id": "F3", "severity": "minor (reproducibility metadata)", "claim": "repro_cmd in run_manifest.json / benchmark.md is executable", "evidence": "`python -m tensorlbm.verification.cavity_re3200 ...` exits 2 with ModuleNotFoundError from both the repo root and TensorLBM/; it only resolves inside run.py's sys.path insertion, and the ambient installed tensorlbm points at the foreign worktree /srv/tensor/agent/work/m21384", "remediation": "publish the repro_cmd as the run.py invocation (auditor-verified working) or set PYTHONPATH=TensorLBM/src in the recorded command"}, {"id": "F4", "severity": "minor (evidence bundle completeness in main)", "claim": "figures ship with the code", "evidence": "git ls-tree -r HEAD | grep re3200/figures -> 0 hits; the two PNGs exist only in /srv/tensor/agent/work/m21790 (filtered by the matured-deliverable commit 990f7e83f). The DB report still carries both figures inline, so the paper-level evidence survives", "remediation": "none required for the verdict; re-add the PNGs if the repo is meant to be self-contained"}], "overstated_claims": ["benchmark.md '## how to reproduce' block: the first bullet (`python benchmarks/verified/cavity/re3200/run.py --n 128 192 256 --steps 150000 ...`) is presented as a reproduce command for the shipped numbers, but no such run exists (only the 6000-step n=128 run does). The published numbers come from the 6000-step run recorded in run_manifest.json argv; the 150k-step grids are still queued.", "No claim of a passing reproduction was made and no L4 level was asserted in the report - that part is clean."], "checks_run": ["psql (tensorplatform): tensor_benchmark_cases anchor REPRO-LBM-HOU1995 -> 0 rows; tensorben